PHASE 3 – WORKING PROTOTYPE

Prototype Overview

The Library Book Checkout System is a simplified web-based prototype developed using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It demonstrates the basic functions needed to manage library books, users, and checkout transactions.

The prototype focuses on the core functionality of viewing books, checking out books, returning books, managing users, and monitoring checkout records.


Implemented Features

1. Dashboard

The Dashboard provides an overview of the library system and displays summary information and recent checkout activities.

2. Books

The Books page displays the available library books and their current status. Books can be identified as available or borrowed.

3. Checkout

The Checkout page allows a user to select a library user and an available book. The system records the checkout date and due date.

4. Return

The Return page displays borrowed books and provides an option to return a book. After a successful return, the book status is changed back to available.

5. Users

The Users page displays the registered library users and their basic information.

6. Local Data Storage

The prototype uses browser localStorage to preserve books, users, and checkout information during use.


Prototype Limitations

The current prototype is designed for demonstration purposes. It does not currently include a backend server, centralized database, strong authentication, authorization, encryption, or server-side validation.

Because localStorage is used, the data is stored locally in the browser. Data changes made in one browser are not automatically shared with other computers or devices.

These limitations will be considered during the threat modeling and secure redesign phases.